{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":297,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","line":582,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[distance functions and segments]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0195}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-segment, lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound}\n\n  \\dcref{ch5:5.3.2b}\n  If $r:U\\to\\mathbb R$ is a smooth distance function on open $U\\subset(M,g)$, the\n  integral curves of $\\nabla r$ are \\emph{segments in $U$}: an integral curve $c$\n  of $\\nabla r$ on $[a,b]$ realises $L(c)|_a^b=r(c(b))-r(c(a))=b-a$ and minimises\n  length among curves in $U$ with the same endpoints.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments}\n  \\sketch\n  Along $\\dot c=\\nabla r$, one has $|\\dot c|=1$ and $dr(\\dot c)=1$, so both\n  $L(c)|_a^b$ and $r(c(b))-r(c(a))$ equal $b-a$.  The bound in\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound} makes every competitor at\n  least this long.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[distance functions and segments] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368352d64697374616e63652d66756e6374696f6e2d7365676d656e7473\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0195</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-segment\">↗ def:pet-ch5-segment</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23lem%3Apet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound\">↗ lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:5.3.2b</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r:U\\to \\mathbb R$\">$r:U\\to \\mathbb R$</span> is a smooth distance function on open <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U\\subset (M,g)$\">$U\\subset (M,g)$</span>, the integral curves of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla r$\">$\\nabla r$</span> are <em>segments in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U$\">$U$</span></em>: an integral curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla r$\">$\\nabla r$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[a,b]$\">$[a,b]$</span> realises <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L(c)|_a^b=r(c(b))-r(c(a))=b-a$\">$L(c)|_a^b=r(c(b))-r(c(a))=b-a$</span> and minimises length among curves in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U$\">$U$</span> with the same endpoints.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23lem%3Apet-ch5-distance-function-segments\">↗ lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments</a> \\sketch Along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dot c=\\nabla r$\">$\\dot c=\\nabla r$</span>, one has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\dot c|=1$\">$|\\dot c|=1$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dr(\\dot c)=1$\">$dr(\\dot c)=1$</span>, so both <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L(c)|_a^b$\">$L(c)|_a^b$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r(c(b))-r(c(a))$\">$r(c(b))-r(c(a))$</span> equal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b-a$\">$b-a$</span>. The bound in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23lem%3Apet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368352d64697374616e63652d66756e6374696f6e2d6c656e6774682d626f756e64\">section 3</a> makes every competitor at least this long. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-rigidity","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment","title":"def:pet-ch5-segment","label":"def:pet-ch5-segment"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound","label":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","label":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics","title":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics","label":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-geodesics"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","label":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-rigidity","title":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-rigidity","label":"rem:pet-ch5-distance-function-rigidity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-minimizer-is-reparametrized-integral-curve","title":"rem:pet-ch5-minimizer-is-reparametrized-integral-curve","label":"rem:pet-ch5-minimizer-is-reparametrized-integral-curve"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#ex:pet-ch5-euclidean-segments","title":"ex:pet-ch5-euclidean-segments","label":"ex:pet-ch5-euclidean-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#ex:pet-ch5-circle-segment","title":"ex:pet-ch5-circle-segment","label":"ex:pet-ch5-circle-segment"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#ex:pet-ch5-sphere-segments","title":"ex:pet-ch5-sphere-segments","label":"ex:pet-ch5-sphere-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-gauss-lemma","title":"lem:pet-ch5-gauss-lemma","label":"lem:pet-ch5-gauss-lemma"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[distance functions and segments]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0195}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-segment, lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound}\n\n  \\dcref{ch5:5.3.2b}\n  If $r:U\\to\\mathbb R$ is a smooth distance function on open $U\\subset(M,g)$, the\n  integral curves of $\\nabla r$ are \\emph{segments in $U$}: an integral curve $c$\n  of $\\nabla r$ on $[a,b]$ realises $L(c)|_a^b=r(c(b))-r(c(a))=b-a$ and minimises\n  length among curves in $U$ with the same endpoints.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-segments}\n  \\sketch\n  Along $\\dot c=\\nabla r$, one has $|\\dot c|=1$ and $dr(\\dot c)=1$, so both\n  $L(c)|_a^b$ and $r(c(b))-r(c(a))$ equal $b-a$.  The bound in\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound} makes every competitor at\n  least this long.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment","title":"def:pet-ch5-segment","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound","title":"lem:pet-ch5-distance-function-length-bound","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}